
                   How to use the Door Statistics Script
                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Introduction:

   I like stats!  I didn't think I had enough going on so I wrote this
script to give information about the online game usage.  For each game it
stores the access count, last time accessed, time spent playing and who
used it last.  The DoorStats.rexx creates a nice bulletin out of the stats
information to add to your stat list...

Installation:

 - Copy DoorStats.rexx to Zeus:Rexx/

 - MakeDir Doors:Stats

 - Edit the Zeus:Rexx/DoorStats.rexx values to suit your system

 - Stick the following bit of code at the beginning of your door menu(s),
   just after the 'Parse Arg Line' bit:

stats.name = ''
stats.last = ''
stats.cont = 0
stats.secs = 0
stats.who  = ''

 - Append the following to the end of your door menu(s):

doori:
	parse arg name

	stats.name = name

	if open( 'file', 'Doors:Stats/'name, 'r' ) then do
		stats.last = readln( 'file' )
		stats.cont = readln( 'file' )
		stats.secs = readln( 'file' )
		stats.who  = readln( 'file' )
		call close( 'file' )
		end

	stats.last = date( 's' ) || ' ' || time( 'n' )
	stats.cont = stats.cont + 1

	GetUserData 'NAME'
	stats.who = RESULT

	return

dooro:
	if stats.name = '' then return

	say time( 'e' )

	stats.secs = stats.secs + trunc( time( 'e' ) )

	if open( 'file', 'Doors:Stats/'stats.name, 'w' ) then do
		call writeln( 'file', stats.last )
		call writeln( 'file', stats.cont )
		call writeln( 'file', stats.secs )
		call writeln( 'file', stats.who  )
		call close( 'file' )
		end

	stats.name = ''
	stats.last = ''
	stats.cont = 0
	stats.secs = 0
	stats.who  = ''

	return

 - For each door you want to create stats on, you need to add a couple of
   lines of code.  Here is an example for 'Hack & Slash':

Option_1:
	call doori( "Hack & Slash" ); call time( 'r' )
	CLIDoor '"Hack&Slash2/HSclient %50|"'
	call dooro()
	Signal MenuLoop

 - The 'call doori( ...' line stores the door name, which will appear in
   the bulletin, and resets the ARexx timer for calculating the time spent
   in the door.  The 'call dooro()' line writes the stats to disk in the
   Doors:Stats/ directory.

 - Run Zeus:Rexx/DoorStats.rexx once a day or add it to your StartUpx.zeus
   scripts...

Chars, al.
